The agency that spent the better part of a decade defining crypto policy through enforcement has published a five-year plan describing blockchain as a technology with &#8220;the potential to revolutionize America's financial infrastructure.&#8221;
The SEC's draft Strategic Plan for fiscal years 2026 through 2030 dedicates a standalone objective to digital assets and blockchain technology, placing the category alongside investor protection, capital formation, and agency modernization.
